   "body": "**Adversarial review round 1 (Fable 5.2, read-only sub-agent of cloud/orch; the author is Opus), verbatim:**\n\n> REQUEST CHANGES\n>\n> Head f781db82 (PR #918, LOT-057). One narrow but demonstrated crash; everything else you asked me to check holds.\n>\n> Findings:\n>\n> 1. **Low — `Packages/HFRKit/Sources/HFRClient/REST/RESTDocument.swift:225`** — `min(position / postsPerPage + 1, topic.pageCount)` traps on server data. Scenario: `RESTDocument.bucket(..., postsPerPage: 1)` on an `R335a` row edited to `last_position` = `Int.max` gives \"Swift runtime failure: arithmetic overflow\" (probe run, process killed). It needs page size 1, which the client accepts (`>= 1`). The same file already guards this class in `summary(of:)` (quotient and remainder). Fix: `min(position / postsPerPage, topic.pageCount - 1) + 1`, plus a test.\n> 2. **Low — `Packages/HFRKit/Sources/HFRClient/REST/RESTBrowsingClient.swift:87`** — mixed sources duplicate rows. Scenario: page 1 falls back to HTML (50 topics), then the caller asks `lastTopics(in:page: 2)` and gets REST rows 26–50 again. Fix: say in the doc comment and the spec that after an `.html` page 1 the caller pages by the HTML navigation.\n> 3. **Detail — `Packages/HFRKit/Sources/HFRClient/REST/RESTDocument.swift:43`** — the comment presents \"REST sub-category `id` = HTML `subcat`\" as a fact. The spec and HFR-PROTOCOL label it a run observation (#285); label it here too. The resume point and read state are labelled correctly in code, spec and protocol.\n>\n> Verified:\n> - **Tests:** `swift test` in `Packages/HFRKit` passes, 2017 tests; SwiftLint is clean on the REST sources and tests.\n> - **Mutations:** five applied and reverted, each failed a named test: fallback after page 1, REST stale-session check, error answer unread, placeholder category/href checks, read-row branch.\n> - **Fixtures:** the URLs and shapes of `R57d`–`R57k`, `R285a`–`R285c` and `R830t` match their meta files and bodies, and each is exercised by a test.\n> - **Error mapping:** `.refused(code:)` (403, 404), `.notFound` (`R57j`) and `.sessionExpired` (`R830t`, only via `confirmStaleSession`) are mapped as the spec says.\n> - **Session:** the anonymous client sends no cookie, the bucket client uses a probe and writes nothing back.\n> - **Boundaries:** REST sources import only Foundation, HFRModels, HFRNetwork and HFRParsing; no app caller exists.\n\nAll three go back to `cloud/lot-057-opus` for one fix commit, followed by a delta review.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
