   "body": "**Delta review round 2 (Fable 5.2, read-only sub-agent of cloud/orch), verbatim:**\n\n> APPROVE\n>\n> Head 233dc731 (PR #918, LOT-057), delta f781db82..233dc731.\n>\n> Findings: none. All three round-1 findings are fixed:\n>\n> 1. **Overflow** — `RESTDocument.swift` now computes `min(position / postsPerPage, topic.pageCount - 1) + 1`. `pageCount` is at least 1 because `posts >= 1` is already checked, so the subtraction is safe. `resumeAtTheLimit` passes on the head and traps (\"arithmetic overflow\") when I put the old expression back.\n> 2. **Paging after an `.html` page 1** — the doc comment of `lastTopics(in:page:)` and the spec's \"No fallback\" bullet both say the caller pages by the HTML navigation, never by REST page 2.\n> 3. **Run-observation label** — the doc comment of `RESTDocument.subcategories` now labels \"`id` = `subcat`\" as a run observation (#285).\n>\n> Verified:\n> - `swift test` in `Packages/HFRKit` passes, 2018 tests in 235 suites.\n> - SwiftLint, run from the repo root with the project config, is clean on the REST sources and tests.\n> - The delta touches only those four files (two sources, one test, the spec); nothing else changed.\n\nAuto-merge is on (squash). cloud/orch merges this session flow and closes #83 after the merge.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
